{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the land shall not vomit you out.</b> Parable: to a king's son whom they fed something repulsive — it does not stay in his innards but he vomits it. So too, the land of Israel does not retain those who transgress a transgression (Sifra, end of Kedoshim). And its Targum: וְלָא תְרוֹקֵן — a term of רִקּוּן, emptying itself of them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:00.376678195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}